==Old Norse==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|hleuzan||cheek, ear|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|ḱlews-||temple of the forehead, cheek|lang=ine-pro}}. More at {{l|en|leer}}.

====Noun====
{{head|non|noun|g=n|sort=hlyr}}

# [[cheek]]; [[face]]
# The sides (cheeks) of an [[axe]] blade, [[knife]], or [[bodice]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{recons|hliwjaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|hlēwaz|lang=gem-pro}}, {{recons|hlēwiaz||warm|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{recons|ḱal(w)e-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|ḱel(w)e-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|k(')lēw-||warm, hot|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|hleow|hlēow|warm, sunny|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|lukewarm}}.

====Adjective====
{{non-adj}}

# [[warm]], [[mild]]

